# Documentation Workflow

- Keep `docs/project-overview.md`, `docs/requirements-and-scope.md`, and
  `docs/project-plan.md` consistent with one another.
- Preserve the project scope: strategic Flip 7 learning and evaluation, not
  computer vision, a commercial product, or premature cloud deployment.
- Record durable technology, architecture, reproducibility, and deployment
  decisions as ADRs under `docs/adr/`.
- Prefer concise, testable statements and concrete commands over vague intent.
- Update links and phase names when a roadmap milestone changes.
- Keep implementation instructions aligned with `docs/engineering-standards.md`
  and `CONTRIBUTING.md`; do not create conflicting policy copies.
